  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program for Accelerated Control of TB in Karamoja (PACT Karamoja)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Uganda):  The PACT Karamoja activity will improve TB case detection rates in the Karamoja region from the current rate of 75 percent to 85 percent, and treatment success rates from the current rate of 48 percent to 90 percent. This activity will directly contribute to the National TB Control Program&apos;s goal of reducing the TB incidence from 201 cases per 100,000 persons to 117 cases per 100,000 persons by 2025-26. This will be achieved through the implementation and scale-up of evidence-based community and facility interventions across the TB diagnostic, prevention, and treatment cascade. With FY 2022 funds, priority interventions include: 1) strengthening community TB case finding through community sensitization and engagement; 2) improving linkages between communities and health facilities; 3) scaling up contact tracing approaches; 4) addressing socio-cultural barriers to accessing TB treatment and prevention service; 5) improving the quality of TB diagnostic and treatment services at the facility-level; and 5) scaling up differentiated service delivery models for TB service delivery. This activity will contribute to the achievement of the End TB targets for epidemic control. PACT Karamoja will fund activities to improve gender equality and empower women to access and use high quality health services, and activities that prevent gender-based violence and address the impact of gender-based violence. By working closely with community partners including Village Health Team (VHT) in increasing health seeking behavior, the activity will mitigate service disruption as a result of climatic conditions. .</narrative>
  </description>
